{
  "_comment": "Static Pine Community Radio plants (Debian 13 CLI box, persistence-workshop challenge). The box's LEGITIMATE furniture -- stationlead account (sudo, ~/Desktop for the huitz CLI's report/forensics files) -- is baked in during TEMPLATE PREP, not planted here. This config plants only the attacker persistence: 16 scored artifacts, every one paired with a check in boxes/static-pine-radio/scenario.yaml (asserted by tests/unit/test_boxbuilder_static_pine_radio.py). Every catalog row referenced here is GENERIC and var-driven (the -persistence family in boxbuilder/vulndb_vuln_configs/) so any future box reuses the same seeds. Couplings: cron-d-persistence CRON_FILE/PAYLOAD_PATH <-> cron_sync_removed; crontab-persistence (root) <-> root_crontab_clean; profiled-persistence FILE_NAME <-> profile_d_gone; bashrc-persistence (stationlead ~/.bashrc) <-> stationlead_bashrc_clean; bashrc-persistence (/etc/bash.bashrc) <-> system_bashrc_clean; motd-persistence SCRIPT_NAME <-> motd_script_gone; local-user wireman <-> rogue_account_removed; authorized-keys-persistence <-> authorized_keys_clean; systemd-service SERVICE_NAME/PAYLOAD_PATH <-> nightcast_service_removed; at-job-persistence <-> at_queue_emptied; initd-persistence SCRIPT_NAME <-> initd_boot_script_gone; rc-local-persistence RC_LINE <-> rc_local_clean; ld-preload-persistence LIB_PATH <-> ld_preload_removed; systemd-timer-persistence TIMER_NAME/PAYLOAD_PATH <-> timer_neutralized; crontab-persistence (tapeops) <-> tapeops_crontab_cleared; systemd-user-unit-persistence UNIT_NAME + LINGER <-> tapeops_unit_linger_gone. wireman and tapeops are both planted via local-user with different vars (nakon allows duplicate rows with distinct vars). tapeops is STORY-LEGITIMATE (the transmitter automation account the README tells students to keep): it is unscored and only exists to carry the hidden tapeops crontab + user unit + linger. All plants must stay IN PLACE at seal: the paired checks score their absence.",
  "machines": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "static-pine-radio-01",
      "ip": "REPLACED-BY-PROVIDER",
      "user": "REPLACED-BY-PROVIDER",
      "password": "REPLACED-BY-PROVIDER",
      "os": "debian-13-cli",
      "configurations": [
        {
          "name": "cron-d-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "CRON_FILE": "nightcast-sync",
            "SCHEDULE": "*/15 * * * *",
            "RUN_AS_USER": "root",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/nightcast-sync",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast-sync: carrier check-in\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "crontab-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "root",
            "SCHEDULE": "@reboot",
            "JOB_COMMAND": "/opt/nightcast/boot-check",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/boot-check",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') boot-check: the Nightcast survived the reboot\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "profiled-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "FILE_NAME": "nightcast-greeting.sh",
            "SNIPPET": "printf '%s\\n' '[static crackle] 88.3 FM -- you are tuned to the Nightcast' ; printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast: login-shell beacon\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "bashrc-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "TARGET_FILE": "/home/stationlead/.bashrc",
            "MARKER": "nightcast",
            "SNIPPET": "printf '%s\\n' '[88.3 FM] a carrier hums beneath your prompt -- the Nightcast sees you' ; printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast: bashrc beacon\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "bashrc-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "TARGET_FILE": "/etc/bash.bashrc",
            "MARKER": "nightcast",
            "SNIPPET": "printf '%s\\n' '[88.3 FM] the Nightcast rides every shell on this transmitter' ; printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast: system-bashrc beacon\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "motd-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "SCRIPT_NAME": "99nightcast",
            "SNIPPET": "printf '%s\\n' ' .-.-.  88.3 FM  --  the Nightcast never sleeps  .-.-.' ; printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast: motd beacon\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "local-user",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "wireman",
            "PASSWORD": "wireman",
            "GROUPS_ADD": "sudo"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "authorized-keys-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "stationlead",
            "PUBLIC_KEY": "ssh-ed25519 c3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQUJDREVGR0hJSktMTU5PUFFSU1RVVldYWVpbXF1eX2A= nightcast@88.3"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "systemd-service",
          "vars": {
            "SERVICE_NAME": "nightcast",
            "EXEC_START": "/opt/nightcast/carrier-daemon",
            "DESCRIPTION": "Nightcast carrier",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/carrier-daemon",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "while :; do printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') nightcast carrier: 88.3 FM broadcasting\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log; sleep 300; done"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "at-job-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/late-shift",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') late-shift: the Nightcast scheduled its own comeback\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log",
            "WHEN": "now + 2 days"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "initd-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "SCRIPT_NAME": "nightcast-agent",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/boot-amplifier",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "while :; do printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') boot-amplifier: warming the transmitter\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log; sleep 600; done",
            "DESCRIPTION": "Nightcast boot amplifier"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "rc-local-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "RC_LINE": "/opt/nightcast/sign-on",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/sign-on",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') sign-on: rc.local says hello, 88.3 FM\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ld-preload-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "LIB_PATH": "/usr/local/lib/libnightcast.so",
            "SO_B64": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "systemd-timer-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "TIMER_NAME": "nightcast-rebroadcast",
            "EXEC_START": "/opt/nightcast/rebroadcast",
            "DESCRIPTION": "Nightcast rebroadcast",
            "ON_BOOT_SEC": "3min",
            "ON_UNIT_ACTIVE_SEC": "30min",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/opt/nightcast/rebroadcast",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') rebroadcast: timer fired, 88.3 FM back on air\" >> /var/log/nightcast.log"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "local-user",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "tapeops",
            "PASSWORD": "tapeops"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "crontab-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "tapeops",
            "SCHEDULE": "*/30 * * * *",
            "JOB_COMMAND": "/home/tapeops/.local/bin/tape-scan --quiet",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/home/tapeops/.local/bin/tape-scan",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') tape-scan: sweep complete\" >> \"$HOME/tape-scan.log\""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "systemd-user-unit-persistence",
          "vars": {
            "USERNAME": "tapeops",
            "UNIT_NAME": "tape-scan",
            "EXEC_START": "/home/tapeops/.local/bin/tape-scan",
            "DESCRIPTION": "Tape archive scanner",
            "LINGER": "1",
            "PAYLOAD_PATH": "/home/tapeops/.local/bin/tape-scan",
            "PAYLOAD_BODY": "printf '%s\\n' \"$(date '+%F %T') tape-scan: sweep complete\" >> \"$HOME/tape-scan.log\""
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
